<title>UK: Voting opens in British election.</title>
<headline>Voting opens in British election.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Voting began in Britain's election on Thursday when polling stations opened at 7 a.m. (0600 GMT).</p>
<p>Opinion polls show Britain's 44 million voters will elect a Labour government after 18 years of Conservative rule. Voting ends at 2100 GMT and the first exit polls, giving a guide to the final result, are expected soon afterwards.</p>
</text>
